The card has fake quotes at lines 92 and 109, using straight double quotes `"..."` (full-width? shows as " in output — let me check actual chars). The lines:

  ```
  > Truman 原话："决定性要素是'必须有'，优化性要素是'来了更好'..."
  ```

  These are curly quotes “ ” (U+201C/201D) or straight? Grep output shows `"决定性要素...` — probably full-width curly quotes “ ”. My _QUOTE_SPAN_RE includes “ ” — yes: `[「“\"]([^」”\"\n]{10,300})[」”\"]`. 

  But the issue: these lines have NO line-number annotation (no L\d+). Per my rule (quote + 行号标注 on same line), they're not checked. The #614 finding says these quotes were packaged as 「Truman 原话+行号」— actually looking at downgrade_reason: "两处加引号「Truman 原话」对源零命中" — the card itself doesn't show行号 in the card body. The task spec says: "卡片正文引号块+标注行号 → grep 源文件必须命中". So quotes annotated with line numbers. But this real card has quotes attributed to "Truman 原话" without L anchors — should those be checked?

  The task spec is explicit: 引号块+标注行号 → must hit. The proposal adds: 加引号且标注「口述/原话/L行号」的内容. So attribution markers include 口述/原话 keywords, not only L-numbers! Proposal: "卡片正文加引号且标注「口述/原话/L行号」的内容，必须在 source_refs 源文件中 grep 命中".

  So my trigger condition should be: line contains L\d+ anchor OR attribution keyword （原话/口述） near the quote. Let me widen: treat a quote as source-claimed if same line contains `L\d` or 原话|口述. Hmm, "口述" appears in various contexts... e.g. "（口述 L2）" typical. But "口述" alone could appear in prose like "口述稿显示". Risk of false positives at WARNING tier is acceptable but noise erodes trust (§3.11 wolf-crying lesson). Compromise: trigger = line matches `L\d{2,}` (line anchors) OR quote immediately preceded/followed by 原话/口述 within short window (same line). 

  For this card, line 92: `> Truman 原话："..."` — 原话 within ~10 chars of quote. Check: does the quote normalize-hit the source? #614 says zero hit — expected WARNING fires. Let me implement: quote is source-claimed if same line has L-anchor, or 「原话」/「口述」within 20 chars before/after the quote span.

  Then the WARNING message should reference the anchor or keyword.

  Also multi-line quote blocks: blockquote quotes can span multiple lines — my line-by-line approach only catches single-line quotes. Line 92's quote is single-line (one long line). Fine for WARNING tier.

